    "created_at": "2018-05-11T02:41:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-05-11T02:41:57Z",
    "body": "> It seems that Firefox only supports the reload override flag for about:blank resources\r\n\r\nI don't believe that's true, last I tested....  We have all sorts of infrastructure to allow reload to reload the actual document.written content, and it's not tied to about:blank in any way I'm aware of.\r\n\r\nConsider this from a user's point of view, by the way.  You load a page.  You click a link, it gets replaced with a totally different page.  You reload; ideally you end up on the \"new\" page.  The modern way to do that is with DOM manipulation and pushstate, but the \"premodern\" way is document.open/write....",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
