    "body": "@annevk So I read the tests a bit more carefully, and the real difference is not about:blank vs not; the real difference is that the test that sets src to `\"/common/blank.html\"` does the `document.write` from the frame's onload event.  The other one does the `document.write` immediately after inserting the iframe in the document.   If you have both use the load event, they have identical behavior.\r\n\r\nNote also that there can well be behavior differences here between iframes and toplevel windows as well as between location.reload() and UI reload...  And it's possible that some of the Firefox behavior got broken recently (e.g. I just filed <https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1460939>).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
